course: dictionary
lesson: 6971
title: Pane: a sheet of glass
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pane is one sheet of glass in a window or a door. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «In everyday life a ball can break a window pane.» A ball hitting glass is a clue: the pane is the glass that breaks.
explain: Pane can also mean a separate part of a window on a screen. A computer screen can show several panes at once, like boxes side by side. The words "screen" and "window" tell you that this pane is not made of glass.
explain: Pane is often used in maths as well. «A window with 3 rows of 4 panes has 12 panes.» To count the panes, multiply the rows by the panes in each row: 3 × 4 = 12. Check your answer by swapping the meaning into the sentence: "a window with 3 rows of 4 sheets of glass" still makes sense.
fact: A pane is one sheet of glass in a window or door.
fact: «Double-glazed windows» have two panes of glass with a layer of trapped air between them.
fact: On a screen, a pane is a separate part of a window.
fact: Pane of glass and window pane are common phrases.
fact: A window with 3 rows of 4 panes has 12 panes in total.
exercise: «A ball broke the window pane.» What is a pane here? | A curtain on a rail | A small bird that sings near the window | A wooden frame around a door | *One sheet of glass in a window or door
exercise: «The classroom window has 3 rows of 4 panes.» How many panes are there in total? | 34 | 43 | 7 | *12
exercise: «Open the second pane on the screen to see your notes.» What does pane mean on a screen? | A bright colour | A picture of a window | *A separate part of a window on a screen | A small button you press to switch off
test: «Double-glazed windows have two panes of glass with air trapped between them.» Why does a double-glazed window have two panes? | To turn the glass into a mirror | To let in more sand | *To trap a layer of air between the glass | To make the window heavier
test: In a Polish greeting, «Dobry dzień, pane», pane is used when calling a man, meaning sir. Is this the same meaning as a window pane? | *No, it is a different meaning, used for a man | Yes, it means a window on a screen | No, it means a row of windows | Yes, it means a sheet of glass
exam: Which sentence uses pane to mean a sheet of glass? | Pani Kowalska and pane Nowak are both coming. | Open the pane to see your notes on the screen. | Dobry dzień, pane Nowak, said the guard. | *The window pane cracked when the ball hit it.
